## Tutorials

A constructor in Java is aspecial methodthat is used to initialize objects.

The constructor is called when an object of a class is created.

It can be used to 
set initial values for object attributes:

Constructors can also take parameters, which is used to initialize 
attributes.

The following example adds anint yparameter 
to the constructor. 
Inside the constructor we set x to y (x=y). When we call 
the constructor, we pass a parameter to the constructor (5), which will set the value of 
x to 5:

You can have as many parameters as you want:

